{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleveque/quantic-agent/pulls/12","id":4788372556,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU_Z6wc8AAAABHWjETA","html_url":"https://github.com/fleveque/quantic-agent/pull/12","diff_url":"https://github.com/fleveque/quantic-agent/pull/12.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/fleveque/quantic-agent/pull/12.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleveque/quantic-agent/issues/12","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleveque/quantic-agent/pulls/12/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleveque/quantic-agent/pulls/12/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleveque/quantic-agent/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleveque/quantic-agent/issues/12/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleveque/quantic-agent/statuses/a1126222317e7e55d44cf3f4001183d3a95938eb","number":12,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Milestone 11: the Dividend Week Ahead — seven locales, data by code, prose without figures","user":{"login":"fleveque","id":568487,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODQ4Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/568487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque","html_url":"https://github.com/fleveque","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`quantic-agent --week-ahead --out DIR` writes next week's Dividend Week Ahead into a folder, one Markdown file per locale (en, es, ca, fr, de, it, pt). Decision [0013](docs/decisions/0013-week-ahead.md).\n\n**Your choices:** public data as it is, so no amounts, raises or radar ([content.md](docs/content.md#the-dividend-week-ahead-as-built) lists what Quantic would need to add); the existing agentic loop for research.\n\n## How it works (`quantic_agent/weekahead.py`)\n\n- **Research**: the agentic loop, asked for the week after today and told today's date.\n- **Data**: code builds the data block from the recorded tool results, then checks it against them (`provenance.check_data`). The model picks the calls, and the run fails in its research phase, resumable, if the week isn't covered or a company in it wasn't looked up.\n- **Prose**: the model writes two sections as JSON (Ollama's `format`, from a Pydantic schema). Any figure, in digits or in words, is named back to it, up to 3 attempts; after that nothing is written (exit 4).\n- **Translations**: each locale is checked on its own, for figures and for a length 0.75–1.75× the English. A failing one is held: not written, kept in the store with its reasons, exit 6.\n- **Files**: the data block is serialised once with every string double-quoted, and all seven files carry it unchanged. Each file is read back before it's written. The run and its posts are recorded first (migration 0005).\n- **Package data**: prompts and the locale table, read with `importlib.resources`. New dependency: PyYAML.\n\n## Measured on live data ([benchmarks](docs/benchmarks/2026-10-08-week-ahead/README.md))\n\n- **Research**: without today's date, 3 of 5 runs asked for a 7-day calendar from a Thursday, and 2 failed. With it, 20 of 20 gathered the whole week.\n- **Prose**: with the final prompt, 10 of 10 runs published, but every one needed 2 or 3 attempts. The writer is shown neutral field names (`long_term_growth`, not `cagr_5y`), which stopped \"five-year\" and \"twelve months\". It still counts the companies (\"two\") whatever the prompt says; the retry is what removes it. This answers design open question 8 for the 9B: with retries, it can.\n- **Translations**: none of 114 was held, and lengths ran 0.95–1.37×. But the Catalan has errors any reader sees. The checks are structural, so whether 5 locales can publish on them alone is now design open question 12, and needs your answer before milestone 12 publishes anything.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Gate: ruff format, ruff check, pyright strict, 317 tests, relative links.\n- 16 guarantees broken on purpose, each failing the test written for it.\n- Built a wheel and loaded the package data from a fresh install.\n\n**Lesson 11:** [formatted page](https://claude.ai/artifact/VFJgaAxgiZx8YiwPFuFBgL) · [code walkthrough](https://claude.ai/artifact/M1FoS3w2xAD3AehxYu7G2u)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T14:32:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T15:22:57Z","closed_at":"2026-10-08T15:22:56Z","merged_at":"2026-10-08T15:22:56Z","merge_commit_sha":"01c8dfd84c74861cade31f8e0689ae725f4e2fcf","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"fleveque:m11-week-ahead","ref":"m11-week-ahead","repo":{"id":1408662209,"node_id":"R_kgDOU_Z6wQ","name":"quantic-agent","full_name":"fleveque/quantic-agent","owner":{"login":"fleveque","id":568487,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODQ4Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/568487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque","html_url":"https://github.com/fleveque","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleveque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.gi